# Development Guidelines

## Core rule

Keep the plugin simple and functional. Add a component or abstraction only
when the current user workflow cannot work without it.

## Implementation

- Build one app component at a time.
- Keep state and operations owned by the component that uses them.
- Prefer direct functions and small adapters over general frameworks.
- Do not copy code from the archived implementation.
- Do not build speculative edge-case handling.

## UI

- Build the UI shell and Settings first.
- Keep visible states clear: loading, empty, ready, and failed.
- Avoid visual complexity that does not improve the common workflow.

## Testing

- Test the component's common workflow first.
- Use temporary repositories for Git behavior.
- Keep source, build, desktop, mobile, remote, and release evidence separate.

## Documentation

- Keep one task per app component.
- Keep implementation notes short and current.
- Record decisions and failures without turning every edge case into a feature.
